================================================================================
FFmpeg (bundled program: resources/engine/bin/ffmpeg, ffprobe)
================================================================================
The desktop app (Linux AppImage, Windows installer) ships FFmpeg's `ffmpeg` and
`ffprobe` executables. They run as separate programs: Hermes Studio starts them
as subprocesses and never links to them. The Hermes Studio code stays MIT.

Build: BtbN FFmpeg-Builds, static "gpl" variant, FFmpeg 9.0 branch
  Version string:  n9.0.2-17-g2a571b6068  (`ffmpeg -version` prints
                   "n9.0.2-17-g2a571b6068-20260930")
  Release:         autobuild-2026-09-30-13-08
                   https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds/releases/tag/autobuild-2026-09-30-13-08
  Linux asset:     https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds/releases/download/autobuild-2026-09-30-13-08/ffmpeg-n9.0.2-17-g2a571b6068-linux64-gpl-9.0.tar.xz
                   sha256 68ee646831adaae2495618346f3bba94ff207ff83bbd34d643e7004730d66269
  Windows asset:   https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds/releases/download/autobuild-2026-09-30-13-08/ffmpeg-n9.0.2-17-g2a571b6068-win64-gpl-9.0.zip
                   sha256 a0e45723c72141975f51d8666302e614711745f3102b704ca3f82c897a58d278

License: GNU General Public License, version 3 or later (GPL-3.0-or-later).
  The build is configured with --enable-gpl --enable-version3. Full text:
  licenses/FFmpeg-GPL.txt (shipped in the app next to this file).
  The build includes GPL-only libraries, among them x264, x265, xavs2, davs2,
  Xvid, vid.stab, Rubber Band, libdvdread/libdvdnav, frei0r and AviSynth, plus
  libass and other LGPL/BSD/MIT libraries. `ffmpeg -version` prints the full
